> They do. All of them. Hyunjun takes the far end. Hanbi takes the arm. Charlie comes last, and room is made for him without anyone having to ask.
@textbox echo
echo: HANBI. HAMIN. SONGHA. CHARLIE. HYUNJUN. HARUTA. JUSTIN. DANIEL. {{playerName}}.
echo: SPECIAL THANKS: SEO YEONHWA. MRS OH, GUITAR. THE CAT, WHO DID NOT MOVE.
@textbox normal
> Nine people watch the names go by to the very end. Your shoulder is against his. It's the easiest thing in the room.
> The screen goes white, then grey. Nobody stands up until somebody wants to.
@fx off
@bg studio_lobby t=fade d=1.4
@call echo_farewell
@bg black t=slow d=2
@music stop
@amb none
> The building is dark, and quiet, and finished. Nine torches find the door.
@if flag.harutax_coat
    > On the step, he holds your coat open for you, as promised. The outside door, not before. You put your arms in. It's only a coat now.
@bg dawn_street t=slow d=2.4
@amb city
@music dawn
@time 05:40
@cam reveal
> The corner store. Not the station one. There's a bench outside, under the awning, still beaded with rain.
> Inside, through the glass, seven people are failing to form a queue. Hyunjun is reading the order off his hand.
@show haruta smile at=c
> Haruta comes out first, carrying a paper bag against his chest with both arms, like something he isn't going to put down for anyone.
> Two egg sandwiches. A strawberry milk. A bag of honey butter chips, unopened, enormous.
@if var.drink == "peach"
    > And a peach iced tea, cold, which he sets on your side of the bench without comment.
@elif var.drink == "choco"
    > And a hot chocolate, the hot kind, which he sets on your side of the bench without comment.
@elif var.drink == "coffee"
    > And a black coffee, no sugar, which he sets on your side of the bench without comment.
@elif var.drink == "grape"
    > And a grape soda, the purple one, which he sets on your side of the bench without comment.
@else
    > And a second strawberry milk, which he sets on your side of the bench with some ceremony.
haruta: I bought a whole bag and I'm not sharing it. {p} Except with you. I've decided that's a different thing from sharing.
> He opens it. The first one goes to you. The second one he eats with his eyes shut.
haruta[smile]: Three years. It's exactly as good as I thought. That almost never happens.
> He wipes his fingers carefully on a napkin, and takes the ledger out of his cardigan.
haruta: I've been thinking about what a person is. "My person." I want to get it right, because I'm going to be one.
haruta[thinking]: I think it's who you tell first. Before you've made it polite. When I want something, I'd like to say it to you while it's still the wrong shape.
you: And when I start looking for my coat, I'll tell you. Before I've put it on.
haruta[smile]: And I won't say "stay." I'll say, "there are hooks." You'll know what I mean.
* [sincere] "I've never had somewhere people expected me back."
    @rel haruta trust+1
    haruta: You have a mark on a practice-room floor with your name on it. And now a bench. It's a start. I'm going to be very boring about it.
* [playful] "Regulars get a loyalty card, I assume."
    @rel haruta closeness+1
    haruta[smile]: Ten Fridays and the eleventh is also a Friday. It's a very simple scheme.
> He opens the ledger on the bench between you. Next Friday's row: his name, your *1*. He writes the date underneath it, the Friday after.
> He doesn't fill in CHOSEN BY. He turns the book round and holds out the pencil on its string.
haruta: We alternate. Down the whole page. I did the sums. It runs out in about a year and a half, and then I'll buy another book.
> You sign. Your name under his. Under that, the columns go on, ruled and empty, and for once an empty row looks like room.
haruta[smile]: I'm happy. I'm saying it out loud, because I say things now. I'm not going anywhere, and I'm not leaving a seat between us.
@sfx bell
> The shop door opens. Hyunjun, holding it with one shoulder. Seven people and too many bags.
> Haruta shifts along the bench until his arm is against yours, and nods at the space that's left.
haruta: Please sit down. I've got an item.
> You stay exactly where you are. It turns out you're good at it.
@ending haruta_beside
@credits
@end

=== haruta_ending_someday
